  "full_response": "Subject: Incident Report - API Key Exposure in Public GitHub Repository\n\n\nDate: April15, 2023\n\n\nBackground: We have detected a security incident which involves potential exposure of API keys related to our payment processing, email services, and cloud on a public GitHub repository. The exposed keys could be used to access sensitive company data and manipulate our services illicitly.\n\n\nIncident Details:\n\n- APICheck ID: 3001\n- Detection Date: April 14, 2023, at 09:45 UTC\n Time detected: Approximately 0150 hours UTC\n- Commit hash: 1a2b3c4d5e6f\n- Repository name: finance/tutoring-services-apis\n- Full repository URL: https://github.com/finance/tutoring-services-apis\n- Last update to the branch with exposed keys: April 13, 2023\n\nThe impacted environments include:\n\n- Payment processing system utilizing Stripe API keys\n- Email service provider using SendGrid API keys\n- Cloud infrastructure managed through AWS, exposed via AWS access keys\n\n\n\nIn response to Discovery:\n\n1. The team involved in this report has immediately initiated the following steps:\n\n   a) Revoke compromised third-party integrations and API keys through respective companies' protocols.\n\n   b) Change all AWS credentials and tighten IAM role permissions.\n\n   c) Perform an internal audit for any suspicious activities within time frame of April 13 - April 14, 2023.\n\n   d) Escalate matter to senior management for additional security measures and support.\n\n\n2. Remediation Steps:\n\n   a) Password reset guidance and security questions for all employee accounts that might have been compromised.\n\n   b) Email profiles and contacts have been updated to prevent unauthorized use of the affected email services.\n\n   c) A full security assessment with identification and mitigation of vulnerabilities.\n\n   d) Communication strategy to stakeholders, customers, and employees regarding the incident (pending internal review).\n\n\nConcluding Remarks:\n\nThe exposed API keys, if misused, could lead to significant financial loss, intellectual property theft, and potentially, legal liabilities. A timeline for the above steps should be strictly followed to limit exposure. Additional investigation will be ongoing while cleanup and remediation will continue. Regular audits will be scheduled to identify any residual impacts of the incident. All findings and progress reports will be communicated to CISO Bob Smith by April 16, 2023.\n\n\nCC: Senior Management, Legal Department, CISO, IT Security Team\n\n\nReport Prepared By: Jane Doe,",
